% PLACEHOLDER MODEL, for demonstration only.
% One fuel block of a prismatic HTGR core (one of the 36 x 5 blocks of the
% core studied in the accompanying paper), with periodic boundary conditions:
% an infinite lattice of identical blocks, so there is no leakage and k_eff
% is the block's k_inf. It is here so that the pipeline can be run end to
% end. Replace it with your own model, keeping the placeholders ba_particles,
% ba_materials, ba_divs, pbed_filename and burnup_days (written between curly
% braces in the cards below; do not write curly braces anywhere else in a
% template, including comments, since the template is filled in with Python's
% str.format).

set title "Placeholder: single HTGR fuel block (36Hx5 design, CCsxFCs = 42x78)"

particle 29
fuel         3.5000E-2
buffer       4.0000E-2
PyC_in       4.3500E-2
SiC          4.7000E-2
PyC_out      5.1000E-2
graphite

{ba_particles}

% Input files for the particle distributions
pbed 900 50 "{pbed_filename}"

%% -- SURFACE definition -- %%
surf 11   hexxprism 0.000 0.000  18.000    0.000  80.000
surf 22   hexxprism 0.000 0.000  18.000    3.000  77.000
surf 55   inf       

surf 99 hexxprism 0.000 0.000 18.000 0.000 80.000   % column boundary, full height

%% -- PIN definition -- %%
pin  UB 
fill 900 0.635
graphite  

pin  GG
graphite

pin  CC
coolant 0.7
graphite

